grantiva runner start       Start the runner with WDA (UIAutomator2 on Android) and keep it alive for interactive use
grantiva runner stop        Stop the running runner session
grantiva runner dump-hierarchy  Dump the view hierarchy from a running app for agent inspection
grantiva mcp                Start the Grantiva MCP server for AI agent integration (tool list: docs/mcp.md)
grantiva init               Generate grantiva.yml (iOS) or grantiva-android.yml (Android) in the current directory
OVERVIEW: Extract or update the embedded runner binary.

A no-op when the installed runner is already this version: it prints "Runner
already installed at <path>", and --json reports "extracted": false.

USAGE: grantiva runner install [--json] [--verbose] [--quiet]

OPTIONS:
  --json                  Output as JSON
  --verbose               Print diagnostic detail (timestamps, labels,
                          metadata) to stderr.
  --quiet                 Silence progress diagnostics on stderr; warnings and
                          errors still print. Program output on stdout is
                          unaffected.
  --version               Show the version.
  -h, --help              Show help information.

OVERVIEW: Start the runner with WDA (UIAutomator2 on Android) and keep it alive
for interactive use.

Without --detach the command stays in the foreground, streams the runner's
output to stderr and holds the session until Ctrl-C (or `grantiva runner stop`
from another shell); it then stops the runner, removes the session files and
releases the device. Interrupted, it exits 130; ended by `grantiva runner stop`
or by a simulator or emulator teardown, it exits 0. With --detach it returns
once the driver is up and the runner keeps the session until `grantiva runner
stop`.

--json prints one document: {"status": "started" | "already_running", "pid":
<number>, "port": <number> (null for a session still starting), "platform":
"ios" | "android", plus "bundleId" and "udid" on iOS or "applicationId" and
"serial" on Android, and "log" with --detach}. "bundle_id" (and "udid" on
Android) are kept for compatibility and are deprecated.

USAGE: grantiva runner start [--json] [--verbose] [--quiet] [--platform <platform>] [--bundle-id <bundle-id>] [--simulator <simulator>] [--application-id <application-id>] [--emulator <emulator>] [--device <device>] [--headless] [--detach]

OPTIONS:
  --json                  Output as JSON
  --verbose               Print diagnostic detail (timestamps, labels,
                          metadata) to stderr.
  --quiet                 Silence progress diagnostics on stderr; warnings and
                          errors still print. Program output on stdout is
                          unaffected.
  --platform <platform>   Target platform: ios or android. Defaults to
                          whichever of grantiva.yml / grantiva-android.yml
                          exists, else the project files in this directory.
                          GRANTIVA_PLATFORM also sets it. (values: ios, android)
  --bundle-id <bundle-id> App bundle identifier (iOS; reads from grantiva.yml
                          if omitted)
  --simulator <simulator> Simulator name or UDID (iOS; reads from grantiva.yml
                          if omitted)
  --application-id <application-id>
                          Application ID (Android; reads from
                          grantiva-android.yml if omitted)
  --emulator <emulator>   AVD name to use, booting it if needed (Android)
  --device <device>       adb serial of an attached emulator or device (Android)
  --headless              Boot an emulator without a window (Android)
  --detach                Detach the runner process from this terminal. Prints
                          the log file path on start.
  --version               Show the version.
  -h, --help              Show help information.

OVERVIEW: Manage the embedded UI automation runner.

USAGE: grantiva runner <subcommand>

OPTIONS:
  --version               Show the version.
  -h, --help              Show help information.

SUBCOMMANDS:
  install                 Extract or update the embedded runner binary.
  version                 Show the embedded runner version.
  start                   Start the runner with WDA (UIAutomator2 on Android)
                          and keep it alive for interactive use.
  stop                    Stop the running runner session.
  dump-hierarchy          Dump the view hierarchy from a running app for agent
                          inspection.

  See 'grantiva help runner <subcommand>' for detailed help.
OVERVIEW: Stop the running runner session.

Stops the session `grantiva runner start` recorded in .grantiva/session.json:
the runner gets SIGINT, then SIGTERM and SIGKILL if it does not exit, and its
session files and device lease are removed. Helpers the runner started for the
device that outlive it (on iOS, the `simctl diagnose` WebDriverAgent's
xcodebuild starts when it is interrupted) are stopped too and listed (`reaped`
in --json); on Android the runner's port forwards and UIAutomator2 server are
cleared. Without one, it releases a `grantiva run --keep-alive` session started
from this directory (every one, if there are several) the way Ctrl-C would, by
sending that grantiva process SIGINT, and waits for it to exit. A run whose
flows had already finished keeps the ready file it wrote (`passed` or
`failed`): the ready file is written once, and the `stopped` result here is the
record of the release. Sessions started from other directories are left alone.
With no session at all it prints "No active session found." and exits 0.

USAGE: grantiva runner stop [--json] [--verbose] [--quiet]

OPTIONS:
  --json                  Output as JSON
  --verbose               Print diagnostic detail (timestamps, labels,
                          metadata) to stderr.
  --quiet                 Silence progress diagnostics on stderr; warnings and
                          errors still print. Program output on stdout is
                          unaffected.
  --version               Show the version.
  -h, --help              Show help information.

